# Where everybody stands.
#
# The engine fills a board depth-first down lane 0, so a party of three arrives in single file
# and so does a wave: leader at (0,0), the two keepers behind it at (0,1) and (0,2). A hold is
# three abreast on the front rank with the dark four ranks away, and nothing but these two verbs
# puts anyone there. There is no host-side call for it either -- `Execute("hold(self, 1)", id, 0)`
# is how the C# game and the Godot node both reach them. FINDINGS #5.
#
# Writing a place is a swap when the slot is taken, so lane goes first and rank second, and the
# order the host calls these in is the order they end up in.

verb hold(who, l):
  who.lane = l
  who.rank = 0

verb arrive(who, l):
  who.lane = l
  who.rank = 3

verb loom(who):
  who.lane = 1
  who.rank = 4
